=== HINT 1: Open maps ===
FILE *f = fopen("/proc/self/maps", "r");

=== HINT 2: Parse perms field ===
char *perms = strchr(line, ' ');
if (perms) {
    perms++;           // skip the space
    if (perms[2] == 'x')
        exec_count++;
}

=== HINT 3: Find notable mappings ===
if (strstr(line, "libc") || strstr(line, "[stack]"))
    printf("Notable: %s", line);  // line already has \n

=== HINT 4: Close ===
fclose(f);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
/proc/<pid>/maps - any process's map (requires ptrace permission).
/proc/self/     - always refers to the calling process.
Other useful /proc/self files:
  status   - name, state, VmRSS, threads, UID
  fd/      - symlinks to every open file descriptor
  cmdline  - null-delimited argv
  environ  - null-delimited environment
  exe      - symlink to executable
  smaps    - per-region detailed memory stats (RSS, PSS, dirty pages)
